;; review4 bug-10: D139's guarantee (a native without a twin raises
;; "lower-wasm: <ns/name> has no twin") does not cover a Java-style static
;; symbol: Integer/parseInt calls through a nil slot and raises a catchable
;; native-looking "TypeError: nil is not a function", review3 bug-07's
;; class. Outside a try the same call raises the named "lower-wasm:
;; Integer/parseInt has no twin" (line 2), so the named stub exists but the
;; call inside the outlined try body takes another path (value call through
;; the nil slot). Other untwinned natives inside try (core/delay*,
;; core/promise in probes/f08) ARE named: the gap is the static-interop form.
;; native lg 4e769212 prints:
;; E: strconv.ParseInt: parsing "x": invalid syntax
;; 42
(println (try (Integer/parseInt "x") (catch Exception e (str "E: " (ex-message e)))))
(println (Integer/parseInt "42"))
